XmlUtil: Load a network disabled for no Internet access as enabled

Releases before this one disabled an Echo's network for good when it had
no Internet access (NETWORK_SELECTION_DISABLED_NO_INTERNET_PERMANENT), and
the disable is saved in WifiConfigStore.xml. Restore it as enabled when
the store loads, as a temporary disable already is, so those Echos rejoin
their network after the update.

diff --git a/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/util/XmlUtil.java b/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/util/XmlUtil.java
index eb204e7..0546946 100644
--- a/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/util/XmlUtil.java
+++ b/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/util/XmlUtil.java
@@ -1076,8 +1076,12 @@ public class XmlUtil {
             // If either of the above codes are invalid or if the network was temporarily disabled
             // (blacklisted), restore the status as enabled. We don't want to persist blacklists
             // across reboots.
+            // Kiosk Satellite Edition: a network disabled for having no Internet access is
+            // enabled again too. Releases before this one disabled it for good on an Echo's
+            // network without Internet access. Nothing on the Echo turns it back on.
             if (status == -1 || disableReason == -1 ||
-                    status == NetworkSelectionStatus.NETWORK_SELECTION_TEMPORARY_DISABLED) {
+                    status == NetworkSelectionStatus.NETWORK_SELECTION_TEMPORARY_DISABLED
+                    || disableReason == NetworkSelectionStatus.DISABLED_NO_INTERNET_PERMANENT) {
                 status = NetworkSelectionStatus.NETWORK_SELECTION_ENABLED;
                 disableReason = NetworkSelectionStatus.DISABLED_NONE;
             }
